A car travels $15$ m while the driver reacts to a hazard, then another $28$ m while braking. Calculate the stopping distance.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm]
\definecolor{reactionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{brakingRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[->,thick,black] (0,0.9) -- (8,0.9);
\path (4,0.9) node[above,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] {Stopping distance};
\draw[->,thick,reactionBlue] (0,0) -- (3,0);
\draw[->,thick,brakingRed] (3,0) -- (8,0);
\path (1.5,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] {Reaction: 15 m};
\path (5.5,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] {Braking: 28 m};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
